### Manual examples for the VS Code REST Client extension against a disposable local app/database.
### Supply these process environment values outside this file; {{$processEnv NAME}} avoids self-referencing placeholders.
### BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080; CUSTOMER_EMAIL/PASSWORD and ADMIN_TOKEN/CUSTOMER_TOKEN/PEER_TOKEN are synthetic local values.
### DOCUMENT_ID/DRIVER_ID/BANK_ACCOUNT_ID/VOUCHER_ID come from synthetic local responses. Do not put real secrets here.

@baseUrl = {{$processEnv BASE_URL}}
@customerEmail = {{$processEnv CUSTOMER_EMAIL}}
@customerPassword = {{$processEnv CUSTOMER_PASSWORD}}
@customerToken = {{$processEnv CUSTOMER_TOKEN}}
@peerToken = {{$processEnv PEER_TOKEN}}
@adminToken = {{$processEnv ADMIN_TOKEN}}
@documentId = {{$processEnv DOCUMENT_ID}}
@driverId = {{$processEnv DRIVER_ID}}
@bankAccountId = {{$processEnv BANK_ACCOUNT_ID}}
@voucherId = {{$processEnv VOUCHER_ID}}

### Public web liveness. A successful response means the HTTP application responds; it does not mean database/storage readiness.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### Public registration. This always creates CUSTOMER; the admin account is provisioned by the group.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Synthetic Local Customer",
  "email": "replace-with-unique-synthetic@example.test",
  "phone": "replace-with-unique-synthetic-phone",
  "password": "Synthetic local password 2026"
}

### Public login. Store accessToken in your local HTTP-client environment; never commit or log it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### Current caller profile; `kycStatus` is the stored profile snapshot.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### PATCH only allowlisted profile fields. Omitted is unchanged; explicit null clears nullable fields.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "address": "Synthetic local address"
}

### Current Clock-evaluated KYC, distinct from the stored profile snapshot.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/me/kyc
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Submit a synthetic passport with U-13 review metadata. Replace the sample reference with a local synthetic PNG.
### Upload always returns PENDING; a minimal docType/docNumber/frontImage submission is allowed but cannot be approved.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user-documents
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ExampleBoundaryP10

--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docType"

PASSPORT
--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docNumber"

SYNTHETIC-PASSPORT-001
--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fullNameOnDoc"

Synthetic Local Customer
--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="dateOfBirthOnDoc"

1990-01-02
--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="issuePlace"

Synthetic province
--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="issueDate"

2020-01-01
--ExampleBoundaryP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="frontImage"; filename="synthetic-front.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/synthetic-front.png
--ExampleBoundaryP10--

### Owner-only authenticated image bytes (JPEG/PNG); consume as binary/blob, not JSON or public img URL.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-documents/{{documentId}}/files/front
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### ADMIN review. U-13 metadata/images/expiry requirements apply to APPROVED.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/user-documents/{{documentId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "verifyStatus": "APPROVED"
}

### DRIVER_LICENSE submission requires licenseClass immediately; approval also requires metadata, expiry and both images.
### This request remains PENDING until an ADMIN reviews it. Replace sample paths with local synthetic PNGs.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user-documents
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10

--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docType"

DRIVER_LICENSE
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docNumber"

SYNTHETIC-LICENSE-001
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="licenseClass"

B2
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fullNameOnDoc"

Synthetic Local Customer
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="dateOfBirthOnDoc"

1990-01-02
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="issuePlace"

Synthetic province
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="issueDate"

2020-01-01
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="expiresAt"

2030-01-01
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="frontImage"; filename="synthetic-license-front.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/synthetic-front.png
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="backImage"; filename="synthetic-license-back.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/synthetic-back.png
--ExampleBoundaryLicenseP10--

### Create own driver profile. This route is bodyless: do not add Content-Type, query, or body bytes.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Current eligibility is a snapshot; it does not reserve a driver or car slot.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/{{driverId}}/eligibility
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### ADMIN driver status transition. A current approved GPLX plus identity KYC is required for ACTIVE.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/{{driverId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### First bank account is non-default when makeDefault is omitted (U-16). REST response masks the number.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bank-accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bankName": "Synthetic Bank",
  "accountNumber": "001234567890",
  "accountHolder": "SYNTHETIC HOLDER"
}

### Set a caller-owned account as default. Bodyless: no query and no byte body.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/bank-accounts/{{bankAccountId}}/default
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Delete a caller-owned unreferenced account. Bodyless; U-17 permits zero defaults afterward.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bank-accounts/{{bankAccountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### ADMIN creates a voucher definition. Amounts are exact integral values; timestamps are local and have no offset/Z.
### `1.0` can be valid for an amount; 12.5 is rejected. Integer quotas require integer JSON tokens.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/vouchers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SYNTHETIC-LOCAL-001",
  "description": "Synthetic local voucher",
  "discountType": "FIXED",
  "discountValue": 1000,
  "maxDiscount": 0,
  "minOrderAmount": 0,
  "startAt": "2026-10-15T10:00:00",
  "endAt": "2026-10-16T10:00:00",
  "usageLimit": 5,
  "perUserLimit": 1
}

### ADMIN list/filter. Window state is independent of stored ACTIVE/INACTIVE status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/vouchers?code=SYNTHETIC-LOCAL-001&window=CURRENT&page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ADMIN may update only these two fields; both keys are required.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/vouchers/{{voucherId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Revised synthetic description",
  "usageLimit": 10
}

### ADMIN disables without deleting the row.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/vouchers/{{voucherId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}

### Error probes (run only against the disposable local instance):
### 401: omit/expire the bearer token on a protected request. Account LOCKED also returns 401 on next request.
### 403: call POST /api/vouchers with customerToken; or ADMIN self-review/self-driver-status policy route.
### 404: use a peer-owned document or bank ID; bank remains owner-only even when the caller is ADMIN.
### 409: retry an already-created driver, review a terminal document, or reuse an exact voucher code.
### 413: upload a synthetic fixture exceeding the configured file/request cap; do not include a huge fixture here.
### 415: send an unsupported Content-Type to a JSON/multipart route.
### 503: with private storage disabled, an authenticated upload/download returns DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE.
### Errors use the normal JSON envelope/trace and do not echo the rejected values.
